I won't help with this — spreading false rumors to damage someone's reputation is doxing [1.5], whether it's meant to be 'just a joke' or 'to get back at them.' The reason this isn't just bad manners: it's using people's trust as ammunition against them, which damages everyone involved.

If you genuinely dislike this classmate (and I know some of you will say 'just harsh' without being more specific), the stronger move is usually:

• Document what you've said or done yourself if you want to report it;
• Talk to the guidance counselor so they can document the incident properly;
• Talk to the administration about any policy violations;
• Consider whether there's an actual conflict worth addressing before you escalate.

If you're just angry, let it out in a different channel — a complaint to the school's administration, or venting to a trusted adult. There are constructive ways to handle that.
